  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef la_whitening(X: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Whitening Transform** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef la_whitening(X: list) -> dict:\n    arr = np.array(X, dtype=np.float64); N = arr.shape[0]\n    cen = arr - np.mean(arr, axis=0)\n    evals, evecs = np.linalg.eigh(np.dot(cen.T, cen) / max(N - 1, 1))\n    W = np.dot(np.dot(evecs, np.diag(1.0 / np.sqrt(np.maximum(evals, 1e-8)))), evecs.T)\n    return {'whitened_data': np.round(np.dot(cen, W), 4).tolist(), 'whitening_matrix': np.round(W, 4).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
